content.text:
Now add `buildLocationDecor`, `buildStars`, `buildCelestial`, `setLocation` methods. Insert after buildScenery or before buildGrandstand. Let's insert after buildScenery before buildGrandstand. Need to write robust code.

Let's define buildLocationDecor:
```
buildLocationDecor() {
  const bounds...
  this.decor = {};
  this.decor.neon = this.buildCity();
  this.decor.alpine = this.buildMountains();
  this.decor.canyon = this.buildMesas();
  this.buildStars();
  this.buildCelestial();
}
```

City: perimeter placement. Need avoid using `this.track.nearest` for each building? 70*480 ~ 33k checks, fine at build. Simpler place outside bounds so no conflict:
- bounds width ~ maybe minX around 400, maxX 2200, minY 400, maxY 1250. Place on rectangle expanded 420-900. Since forest border is near bounds, city behind.
```
const ring = [
 {x:..., z: bounds.minY - 260 - rnd()*420, w...},
 ...
]
```
Avoid corners. We'll generate 64. Use side 0..3. Materials two. Use instanced? Use individual mesh for ease and different heights. 64 draw calls per location group hidden usually. Fine but hidden group still draws 0. 2 materials means 64 draw calls when neon selected, acceptable. Could use instancing for performance. Let's use two InstancedMesh groups with per-instance color. But emissive map and per-instance color; instance color affects diffuse only, windows map multiplies. The emissive stays same cyan/magenta based on material. Two groups gives variation. We'll use InstancedMesh with a unit box geometry. Each building is an instance with scale and rotation. Need color per instance for tone. makeInstanced supports colors and rotation, scale. Great.

For each building item:
```
{ x, z, y: h/2, sx: w, sy:h, sz:d, rot: 0, color: new THREE.Color(...) }
```
But makeInstanced sets rotation.y and scale. Good. Use two arrays: `cityCyan`, `cityMagenta`.
Material:
```
const matA = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color:0xffffff, map: windowTex, emissive:0x7fdcff, emissiveMap: windowTex, emissiveIntensity:1.6, roughness:0.72, metalness:0.28 });
```
Wait using same map and emissiveMap: diffuse map dark with colored windows; emissive map also colored windows, added. Good. Color per instance multiplies diffuse and maybe not emissive. Fine.
Use `makeInstanced(new THREE.BoxGeometry(1,1,1), matA, cityA)`.
Add rooftop glow: maybe not.
City group add both meshes. Set visible false later.

Mountains:
```
const mountainItems = [];
const capItems = [];
for i<30:
 angle = i/30*TAU + rnd*0.1; radius = 1900 + rnd*600;
 x = cx+cos*radius*1.25; z = cz+sin*radius*0.85;
 h=260+rnd*520; base=240+rnd*300; // cone geo 1 height centered at .5? ConeGeometry(1,1) centered at 0 with height 1 -> y from -0.5..0.5. Set y = h/2.
 item {x,z,y:h/2-20,sx:base,sy:h,sz:base, rot:..., color: Color(0x5b7c99...) }
 cap {x,z,y:h-? ... sx:base*0.36, sy:h*0.28, sz:base*0.36, color white}
```
But instanced cone scaling with unit geometry: `ConeGeometry(1, 1, 7)` has radius 1, height 1. scale x/z=base, y=h. Good. Cap at top: If cone base at y=0 and tip at y=h, cap cone should sit near tip with smaller scale and be positioned appropriately. A smaller white cone with base at y = h*0.52 and height h*0.55 would cover upper part. Set y = h*0.72, sy=h*0.58, sx=base*0.44, sz=base*0.44. Its base at h*0.72 - h*0.29 = h*0.43; tip at h*1.01. Not exact but looks like snowcap. Good.
Colors: base `0x4a647d` blue-gray, cap `0xe8f4ff`. With per-instance color.
Add maybe smaller foothills dark. Keep 26.

Mesas:
```
items {x,z,y:h/2,sx:r,sy:h,sz:r, rot, color}
cyl geo (0.72,1,1,7)
```
Place around ring at radius 1600-2400. Colors 0x9a4f2f, 0xb86b3f, 0x8a4429 plus dusty. Add top cap? Cylinder top face already same color. Maybe add a thin lighter top disc instanced? Could add a second mesh with CylinderGeometry(0.72,0.72,0.02,7) scaled r and height 1 at y=h; color lighter. Not necessary.

Stars:
- Use positions in world. Ensure PointsMaterial fog false, size maybe 9.
- Determine center from bounds. `radius 4300`, upper hemisphere. Some stars behind.
- `this.stars.material.opacity` set by loc.stars. `visible = loc.stars > 0`.
- Color maybe 0xd9e8ff.

Celestial:
- Sprite material with GLOW_TEX and additive. Position based on loc celestial.
- `this.celestial = new THREE.Sprite(mat); this.celestial.scale.set(1000,1000,1); this.scene.add(...)`.
- In setLocation, scale and position, color, opacity.
- For non-night, sun position; for night moon/glow.

Location group visibility and material application:
```
setLocation(idOrLoc) {
 const loc = typeof idOrLoc === 'string' ? getLocation(idOrLoc) : idOrLoc;
 this.location = loc;
 const t = this.theme;
 this.skyMat.uniforms...
 this.scene.fog.color.set(loc.fog.color); near/far
 this.renderer.toneMappingExposure = loc.exposure;
 this.postfx.setLook({
   exposure: loc.exposure,
   bloomStrength: loc.bloom.strength,
   blurPixels: 1.35,
   blurRadius: loc.bloom.radius,
   threshold: loc.bloom.threshold,
   knee: loc.bloom.knee,
 });
 // lights
 ...
 // ground
 t.ground.map = this.groundMaps[loc.ground.kind];
 t.ground.color.set(loc.ground.tint);
 t.ground.needsUpdate = true;
 t.outerGround.color.set(loc.ground.outer);
 // track
 t.road.color.set(loc.road.tint); roughness/metalness
 t.shoulder.color.set(loc.shoulder);
 t.line.color.set(loc.line);
 t.line.emissive.set(loc.line);? make emissive maybe scaled. Better `t.line.emissive.set(new THREE.Color(loc.line).multiplyScalar(0.12))` but Color constructor. We can set color. 
 t.rail.color.set(loc.rail);
 t.kerb.color.set(loc.kerb);
 t.post.color.set(...). We don't have post color in config; use rail darkened. Could just set white? `t.post.color.set(loc.night ? 0x1c2630 : 0x3d4a49)`. Hmm config no post. Use `new THREE.Color(loc.rail).multiplyScalar(0.55)`. Need avoid allocating each switch? only on switch. Fine.
 t.reflector.emissive.set(loc.accent); intensity night 1.2 else 0.4.
 // ramps
 t.rampRail.color.set(loc.rampRail); emissive.set(loc.rampGlow); intensity night? etc
 t.rampLip.color.set(loc.rampLip); emissive.set(loc.rampGlow); intensity = loc.night ? 2.4 : 1.8
 t.rampBase.color.set(loc.rampRail)
 // scenery tints
 t.leaf.color.set(loc.leafTint); t.trunk... rock...
 // decor
 for (const [key, group] of Object.entries(this.decor)) group.visible = key === loc.props;
 // stars
 if (this.stars) { this.stars.visible = loc.stars > 0; this.stars.material.opacity = clamp(loc.stars / 1200, 0.35, 0.95); }
 // celestial
 ...
}
```
But `this.decor` values may be null; skip.

Line material emissive: current is 0x2a2a22. We can set `t.line.emissive.set(loc.line); t.line.emissiveIntensity = loc.night ? 0.55 : 0.18;` That makes lines glow at night. Nice bloom.

Kerb material has vertex colors; setting material.color multiplies. loc.kerb can be near white / tinted.

Postfx blur: The "small amount overall" constant. Keep `blurPixels: 1.35`. Maybe increase slightly on bigger screens? Use 1.35.

Location-specific `road` roughness etc.

`t.ground.map` may require map.needsUpdate? only if undefined. Set `t.ground.needsUpdate = true` safe.

`this.scene.fog` color. Note `Fog` color object in linear; set with hex converts to linear. good.

`this.skyMat.uniforms` colors set.

Now add methods.

input.newString:
buildLocationDecor() {
  this.decor = {
    ridge: null,
    neon: this.buildNeonCity(),
    alpine: this.buildAlpinePeaks(),
    canyon: this.buildCanyonMesas(),
  };
  this.buildStars();
  this.buildCelestial();
}

buildNeonCity() {
  const bounds = this.track.bounds;
  const rnd = mulberry32(771);
  const windowTexture = makeWindowTexture();
  const group = new THREE.Group();
  group.visible = false;

  const cyan = [];
  const magenta = [];
  const palette = [0x2b3d63, 0x24304f, 0x354166, 0x1e2946, 0x3b3260];

  for (let i = 0; i < 72; i++) {
    const side = i % 4;
    const along = rnd();
    const inset = 320 + rnd() * 680;
    const width = 60 + rnd() * 110;
    const depth = 60 + rnd() * 110;
    const height = 130 + rnd() * 460;
    let x;
    let z;
    if (side === 0) {
      x = bounds.minX + along * (bounds.maxX - bounds.minX);
      z = bounds.minY - inset;
    } else if (side === 1) {
      x = bounds.minX + along * (bounds.maxX - bounds.minX);
      z = bounds.maxY + inset;
    } else if (side === 2) {
      x = bounds.minX - inset;
      z = bounds.minY + along * (bounds.maxY - bounds.minY);
    } else {
      x = bounds.maxX + inset;
      z = bounds.minY + along * (bounds.maxY - bounds.minY);
    }
    const item = {
      x,
      z,
      y: height / 2 - 0.4,
      sx: width,
      sy: height,
      sz: depth,
      rot: 0,
      color: new THREE.Color(palette[Math.floor(rnd() * palette.length)]),
    };
    if (rnd() < 0.5) cyan.push(item);
    else magenta.push(item);
  }

  const makeCityMaterial = (emissive) =>
    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({
      color: 0xffffff,
      map: windowTexture,
      emissive,
      emissiveMap: windowTexture,
      emissiveIntensity: 1.55,
      roughness: 0.74,
      metalness: 0.24,
    });

  const cyanMesh = makeInstanced(
    new THREE.BoxGeometry(1, 1, 1),
    makeCityMaterial(0x7fe8ff),
    cyan
  );
  const magentaMesh = makeInstanced(
    new THREE.BoxGeometry(1, 1, 1),
    makeCityMaterial(0xff6ad5),
    magenta
  );
  if (cyanMesh) group.add(cyanMesh);
  if (magentaMesh) group.add(magentaMesh);

  // Rooftop beacons give the skyline a few bright points for the bloom.
  const beaconMaterial = new THREE.SpriteMaterial({
    map: GLOW_TEX,
    color: 0x8ff6ff,
    transparent: true,
    opacity: 0.85,
    depthWrite: false,
    blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,
  });
  for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    const item = [...cyan, ...magenta][Math.floor(rnd() * (cyan.length + magenta.length))];
    if (!item) continue;
    const beacon = new THREE.Sprite(beaconMaterial);
    beacon.position.set(item.x, item.sy + 10, item.z);
    beacon.scale.set(34, 34, 1);
    group.add(beacon);
  }

  this.scene.add(group);
  return group;
}

buildAlpinePeaks() {
  const bounds = this.track.bounds;
  const cx = (bounds.minX + bounds.maxX) / 2;
  const cz = (bounds.minY + bounds.maxY) / 2;
  const rnd = mulberry32(5533);
  const group = new THREE.Group();
  group.visible = false;

  const peaks = [];
  const caps = [];
  const peakColors = [0x4d6684, 0x5a738f, 0x405a76, 0x627c97];
  for (let i = 0; i < 28; i++) {
    const angle = (i / 28) * TAU + (rnd() - 0.5) * 0.16;
    const radius = 1750 + rnd() * 900;
    const x = cx + Math.cos(angle) * radius * 1.22;
    const z = cz + Math.sin(angle) * radius * 0.82;
    const height = 300 + rnd() * 620;
    const base = 260 + rnd() * 360;
    peaks.push({
      x,
      z,
      y: height / 2 - 40,
      sx: base,
      sy: height,
      sz: base,
      rot: rnd() * TAU,
      color: new THREE.Color(peakColors[Math.floor(rnd() * peakColors.length)]),
    });
    caps.push({
      x,
      z,
      y: height * 0.7,
      sx: base * 0.43,
      sy: height * 0.58,
      sz: base * 0.43,
      rot: rnd() * TAU,
      color: new THREE.Color(0xe7f2ff),
    });
  }

  const peakMesh = makeInstanced(
    new THREE.ConeGeometry(1, 1, 7),
    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({
      color: 0xffffff,
      roughness: 0.94,
      flatShading: true,
    }),
    peaks
  );
  const capMesh = makeInstanced(
    new THREE.ConeGeometry(1, 1, 7),
    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({
      color: 0xffffff,
      roughness: 0.82,
      flatShading: true,
    }),
    caps
  );
  if (peakMesh) group.add(peakMesh);
  if (capMesh) group.add(capMesh);

  this.scene.add(group);
  return group;
}

buildCanyonMesas() {
  const bounds = this.track.bounds;
  const cx = (bounds.minX + bounds.maxX) / 2;
  const cz = (bounds.minY + bounds.maxY) / 2;
  const rnd = mulberry32(8821);
  const group = new THREE.Group();
  group.visible = false;

  const mesas = [];
  const colors = [0x9d4f30, 0xb8653d, 0x8d452b, 0xc47a4d, 0xa65436];
  for (let i = 0; i < 32; i++) {
    const angle = (i / 32) * TAU + (rnd() - 0.5) * 0.2;
    const radius = 1550 + rnd() * 1000;
    const x = cx + Math.cos(angle) * radius * 1.2;
    const z = cz + Math.sin(angle) * radius * 0.84;
    const height = 110 + rnd() * 330;
    const base = 190 + rnd() * 340;
    mesas.push({
      x,
      z,
      y: height / 2 - 30,
      sx: base,
      sy: height,
      sz: base,
      rot: rnd() * TAU,
      color: new THREE.Color(colors[Math.floor(rnd() * colors.length)]),
    });
  }

  const mesaMesh = makeInstanced(
    new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.68, 1, 1, 7),
    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({
      color: 0xffffff,
      roughness: 0.96,
      flatShading: true,
    }),
    mesas
  );
  if (mesaMesh) group.add(mesaMesh);

  // A handful of glowing dust sprites catch the low sun.
  const dustMaterial = new THREE.SpriteMaterial({
    map: GLOW_TEX,
    color: 0xffb36b,
    transparent: true,
    opacity: 0.24,
    depthWrite: false,
    blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,
  });
  for (let i = 0; i < 14; i++) {
    const item = mesas[Math.floor(rnd() * mesas.length)];
    if (!item) continue;
    const sprite = new THREE.Sprite(dustMaterial);
    sprite.position.set(
      item.x + (rnd() - 0.5) * 300,
      40 + rnd() * 180,
      item.z + (rnd() - 0.5) * 300
    );
    sprite.scale.set(240 + rnd() * 260, 160 + rnd() * 160, 1);
    group.add(sprite);
  }

  this.scene.add(group);
  return group;
}

buildStars() {
  const bounds = this.track.bounds;
  const cx = (bounds.minX + bounds.maxX) / 2;
  const cz = (bounds.minY + bounds.maxY) / 2;
  const rnd = mulberry32(31337);
  const positions = [];
  const sizes = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < 1700; i++) {
    const theta = rnd() * TAU;
    const phi = Math.acos(0.05 + rnd() * 0.95);
    const radius = 4350;
    positions.push(
      cx + Math.cos(theta) * Math.sin(phi) * radius,
      Math.cos(phi) * radius + 260,
      cz + Math.sin(theta) * Math.sin(phi) * radius
    );
    sizes.push(0.55 + rnd() * 1.4);
  }
  const geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
  geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(positions, 3));
  geometry.setAttribute('size', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(sizes, 1));

  this.stars = new THREE.Points(
    geometry,
    new THREE.PointsMaterial({
      color: 0xdcecff,
      size: 10,
      sizeAttenuation: true,
      transparent: true,
      opacity: 0.75,
      depthWrite: false,
      fog: false,
      blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,
    })
  );
  this.stars.frustumCulled = false;
  this.stars.visible = false;
  this.scene.add(this.stars);
}

buildCelestial() {
  this.celestial = new THREE.Sprite(
    new THREE.SpriteMaterial({
      map: GLOW_TEX,
      color: 0xffffff,
      transparent: true,
      opacity: 0.8,
      depthWrite: false,
      fog: false,
      blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,
    })
  );
  this.celestial.frustumCulled = false;
  this.scene.add(this.celestial);
}

setLocation(idOrLocation) {
  const loc = typeof idOrLocation === 'string' ? getLocation(idOrLocation) : idOrLocation;
  if (!loc) return;
  this.location = loc;

  const bounds = this.track.bounds;
  const cx = (bounds.minX + bounds.maxX) / 2;
  const cz = (bounds.minY + bounds.maxY) / 2;

  this.skyMat.uniforms.topColor.value.set(loc.sky.top);
  this.skyMat.uniforms.horizonColor.value.set(loc.sky.horizon);
  this.scene.fog.color.set(loc.fog.color);
  this.scene.fog.near = loc.fog.near;
  this.scene.fog.far = loc.fog.far;

  // Keep the renderer exposure in sync even though the composite shader
  // owns the actual tone mapping for the post chain.
  this.renderer.toneMappingExposure = loc.exposure;
  this.postfx.setLook({
    exposure: loc.exposure,
    bloomStrength: loc.bloom.strength,
    blurPixels: 1.35,
    blurRadius: loc.bloom.radius,
    threshold: loc.bloom.threshold,
    knee: loc.bloom.knee,
  });

  this.hemiLight.color.set(loc.hemi.sky);
  this.hemiLight.groundColor.set(loc.hemi.ground);
  this.hemiLight.intensity = loc.hemi.intensity;
  this.sunLight.color.set(loc.sun.color);
  this.sunLight.intensity = loc.sun.intensity;
  this.sunLight.position.set(...loc.sun.position);
  this.fillLight.color.set(loc.fill.color);
  this.fillLight.intensity = loc.fill.intensity;
  this.ambientLight.intensity = loc.ambient;

  const t = this.theme;
  t.ground.map = this.groundMaps[loc.ground.kind];
  t.ground.color.set(loc.ground.tint);
  t.ground.needsUpdate = true;
  t.outerGround.color.set(loc.ground.outer);

  t.road.color.set(loc.road.tint);
  t.road.roughness = loc.road.roughness;
  t.road.metalness = loc.road.metalness;
  t.shoulder.color.set(loc.shoulder);
  t.line.color.set(loc.line);
  t.line.emissive.set(loc.line);
  t.line.emissiveIntensity = loc.night ? 0.5 : 0.16;
  t.rail.color.set(loc.rail);
  t.kerb.color.set(loc.kerb);
  t.post.color.set(loc.rail).multiplyScalar(loc.night ? 0.42 : 0.62);
  t.reflector.emissive.set(loc.accent);
  t.reflector.emissiveIntensity = loc.night ? 1.1 : 0.4;

  t.rampRail.color.set(loc.rampRail);
  t.rampRail.emissive.set(loc.rampGlow);
  t.rampRail.emissiveIntensity = loc.night ? 2.2 : 1.15;
  t.rampLip.color.set(loc.rampLip);
  t.rampLip.emissive.set(loc.rampGlow);
  t.rampLip.emissiveIntensity = loc.night ? 2.8 : 1.9;
  t.rampBase.color.set(loc.rampRail);

  t.leaf.color.set(loc.leafTint);
  t.trunk.color.set(loc.trunkTint);
  t.rock.color.set(loc.rockTint);
  t.tire.color.set(loc.night ? 0x0d1118 : 0x171b1e);

  for (const [key, group] of Object.entries(this.decor)) {
    if (group) group.visible = key === loc.props;
  }

  if (this.stars) {
    this.stars.visible = loc.stars > 0;
    this.stars.material.opacity = clamp(loc.stars / 1500, 0.32, 0.92);
  }

  if (this.celestial) {
    const c = loc.celestial;
    const dir = new THREE.Vector3(...c.position).normalize();
    this.celestial.position.set(
      cx + dir.x * 4100,
      Math.max(420, dir.y * 4100),
      cz + dir.z * 4100
    );
    this.celestial.scale.set(c.size, c.size, 1);
    this.celestial.material.color.set(c.color);
    this.celestial.material.opacity = c.opacity;
    this.celestial.material.color.multiplyScalar(c.power);
    this.celestial.material.needsUpdate = true;
  }
}

