```

Method:

```
  tintScenery(loc) {
    if (!this.scenery) return;
    const special = loc.id === 'candy' || loc.id === 'haunt' ? this.sceneryPalettes[loc.id] : null;
    for (const [key, entry] of Object.entries(this.scenery)) {
      if (!entry.mesh) continue;
      const palette = special ? special[key] : entry.palette;
      entry.items.forEach((item, index) => {
        const tone = Number.isFinite(item.tone) ? item.tone : 0.5;
        const color = palette[Math.floor(tone * palette.length) % palette.length];
        entry.mesh.setColorAt(index, new THREE.Color(color));
      });
      if (entry.mesh.instanceColor) entry.mesh.instanceColor.needsUpdate = true;
    }
    this.theme.leaf.color.set(special ? 0xffffff : loc.leafTint);
  }
```

Careful: `Math.floor(tone*palette.length)` could equal length when tone = 1, hence % length.

For default (ridge), palette restored to green and leaf material tinted loc.leafTint. Good.

Call in setLocation after `t.leaf.color.set(loc.leafTint);`:
```
this.tintScenery(loc);
```
Note tintScenery references theme.leaf existing. Fine.

Now add method near setLocation.

