content.text:
AI on technical preset gets badly stuck and wall hits, only completing less than a lap in 20s with speeds 9-278. The track length is probably ~10k? It progresses 400 samples means 2/3 of a lap? Actually N=480 samples, prog ~400, so near end of lap. In 20s, lap would be 24s. Wall hits frequent. The chicane barriers and banked curve may be blocking AI or the tight track. The AI is not chicane-aware; it aims at lane center which is blocked. They keep hitting barriers (wallHit 30-40). Some get stuck at speed 2/9/10 for a while.

The preset "Technical Turns" uses a 7x? rectangle 2..8, 0..6: width 7 cells * 300 = 2100, height 6*300=1800. Lap ~7800. AI should do ~15s/lap. They got 400/480 progress in 20s = 0.83 lap, so 24s lap. Slow due to chicanes. Some are stuck.

Need to improve AI awareness of chicane barriers or make barriers less obstructive. AI uses lanePx that can be ±track.width*0.32 (52) around the center. The chicane gap is from -84 to -14 or -14 to 84. An AI targeting lane center (0) hits the wall because barrier covers ±14? For side=1 barrier covers -14..84; the center (0) is inside. If the AI could target -49 in the gap, it would pass. Let's implement barrier avoidance in the AI: look ahead for barriers and steer to the open side.

Simplest: add a `features` reference to AIDriver and compute a lateral target offset that avoids upcoming barriers. But AIDriver only has track. We can pass features to constructor or update. In main, drivers created with `new AIDriver(car, track, ...)`; after track swap we update driver.track. Add `driver.features = features` similarly.

Then in AI update, for the nearest upcoming barrier within ~200 px:
- Each barrier has x,z,tx,ty,side, halfWidth, halfLen, index.
- We want to choose a lateral target on the open side. Since barrier center lateral = side*(W/2-halfWall+2) = ±35; barrier covers center ±49 → on side=+1 covers [-14, +84]; open gap is [-82,-14], target around -48. On side=-1 open gap [14,82], target +48.
- So target offset = -side * (W/2 - halfWall*0.5) maybe -side*58? Use -side*(W*0.3) ≈ -49.
- Blend this into `lanePx` for the pure pursuit target, maybe clamped to gap. If approaching barrier, add an avoid shift.

We can implement in ai.js:
```
if (this.features && this.features.barriers.length) {
  const W = track.width;
  for (const b of this.features.barriers) {
    const ahead = ((b.index - i + N) % N) * track.ds;
    if (ahead > 6 && ahead < 240) {
      const open = -b.side * (W/2 - b.halfWidth * 0.55); // ≈ -49
      // weight strongest when close
      const w = clamp(1 - ahead/240, 0, 1);
      lanePx = lanePx * (1 - w) + open * w; // careful: open sign
      break;
    }
  }
}
```
But lanePx is computed after; we need the barrier target before lanePx. Let's incorporate into lanePx calculation:
```
let chicaneTarget = null;
...
const laneLimit = ...
let lanePx = clamp(this.lane*..., ...)
if (chicaneTarget !== null) lanePx = clamp(lanePx*0.25 + chicaneTarget*0.75, laneLimit...);
```
The barrier's open side target should be inside laneLimit (= W/2-34 = 48). open = -side*(W/2 - halfWall*0.8) = -side*(82-39)= -43. Good. For side=1 → -43 (within -48). For side=-1 → +43.

But if there are multiple barriers in sequence (3 alternating), AI should follow the slalom: the first barrier at index center - step (b.index - 8 samples?) each barrier's own index is stored. Approach each sequentially. The nearest ahead one leads to the gap on the opposite side. Since next barrier alternates side, the AI will switch. Good.

Also the barrier wall's halfLen along tangent ≈ 31; the AI has to be in the gap before reaching it. Start avoidance at 240 px (~8 samples?) Actually ds ~? track length/N. For technical, track length maybe 9000/480=18.75. 240 px = 12.8 samples. Barrier length 26 samples = 487px. Hmm, distance between barriers = round(26/3.4)=8 samples = 150px. So they are close. Starting avoidance at 240 might switch too late/conflicting. Better detect all barriers ahead within ~400 and choose the nearest; but when you're beside one barrier, it's not ahead. The nearest barrier index ahead may be the next one. As you pass, switch. Starting 300 px ahead gives ~16 samples, enough.

Also AI collision walls are resolved by physics.

Let's add features to AI. Need to pass in main constructor and in swapTrack. Search `new AIDriver`.

